well it looks like the universe found  something worse than death being my  mother yes the show that's just about  the only good thing with the name  russian on it at the moment is back with  a new time traveling twist that shakes  up the formula from season one in this  video we'll be taking a look at season  two's ending its timeline and how many  krugerrins it takes to alter the very  fabric of time season two takes place  almost four years after the events of  season one which saw nadia volvokov and  alan zaveri break their groundhog  day-esque time loops and return their  lives back to normal but time isn't done  with them yet whereas season 1 saw our  characters repeat the same day over and  over again season 2 takes a completely  different approach where supernatural  trains transport our characters back and  forth through time but not only that it  transports them into the bodies of  different family members but why is this  happening as nadia's grandmother vera  says in episode 3 there are things in  life that cannot be explained but we're  going to try to explain anyway while  vira nor the show have the answer to the  magical trains portion of this question  what's more important is why this is  happening to nadia in particular in  season one that time loop chose nadia  because of one thing that was holding  her back that was guilt nadia felt  responsible for her mother's death about  a year before her mother nora killed  herself nadia is given the choice to  either live with her mentally unstable  mother or ruth nadia chose ruth and this  culminated in her mother killing herself  hence this guilt season 2 however asks  what if we could fix that if only nadia  could go back in time and change  something so this future never happened  as chez says in episode 2 in our house  oconee island is the thing that would  have made everything better  if only it had happened so what is  nadia's coney island for her it's  retrieving her grandmother's 150 gold  krugerrands worth what she thinks is  about 280 000  by today's standards these are south  african gold coins that her mother stole  from her grandmother and by nadia  bringing them back to her grandmother  she thinks she can close this crazy time  traveling train loop vera chose gold  krugerrins instead of putting the money  in a bank due to her distrust of  government and the banks growing up as a  jew in world war ii hungary she knew how  easy it was for bank accounts to be  frozen money stolen and personal effects  seized these coins could be easily  hidden and because gold isn't tied to a  specific currency their price wouldn't  be in danger of hyperinflation nadia's  attempts at retrieving the coins from  her mother in 1982 prove fruitless she  eventually manages to retrieve them but  when she sees her friend allen on a  similar time traveling train she leaves  them unattended and the bag of coins  vanish it seems whatever force has  brought her into this situation doesn't  want her to mess with time so when nadia  figures out she can go even further back  in time to when her grandmother was in  hungary in 1944 she believes she can get  the coins back yet again and that's  exactly what she does traveling back to  1944 and taking over the body of her  grandmother who has taken the name vera  volvokov in an attempt to hide her  jewish last name peshawar the person who  helps her with this transition also  gives her a cross as it seems vera can  pass for a christian nadia's search  brings her to a storage facility in  budapest where thousands of items  forcefully taken from the jewish  population are resold to the public  veera's family was told they would be  given these items back after the war and  was even issued a receipt which nadia  finds hidden in the back of one of her  family photos this of course was all a  lie but at least this receipt has the  crate number of her family's possessions  you'll notice that the krugerrands  aren't in here that's because the items  stashed in her bag haven't been pawned  yet for them but another problem remains  how does she safely stash these items so  they can be retrieved by her grandmother  years later this is where laszlo kiss  comes in he's a hungarian priest who  nadia saw a grave of in 2022 hungary  covered in small rocks a jewish custom  because laszlo wasn't jewish it could be  assumed he was a friend of the jews due  to these rocks placed on his grave nadia  makes reference to this being done to  oscar schindler's grave in schindler's  list so nadia stashes her family's  possessions in what appears to be some  sort of sewer and gives the map to its  location to laszlo to give to her  grandmother after the war and that's  exactly what happens the very first shot  of the season is vera retrieving the bag  of possessions nadia stashed away  decades earlier but all of this hasn't  solved anything in fact by meddling in  the past all nadia has done is create  the very future she sought to disrupt  she is caught in another time loop one  in which everything she does leads to  the same outcome turns out  couldn't change anything at all so i i  can only do what was always done so  nadia has one last hail mary of a plan  in 1982 she's in control of her pregnant  mother when she has the baby ironically  on the platform of a train station what  if she took the child back to 2022 with  her that way she could be her own mother  and give her the mom she wished she had  as you can imagine this goes terribly  wrong as the very fabric of time itself  starts to collapse when nadia emerges  back in 2022 with the baby she  experiences multiple timelines as if  time has fragmented into multiple  potential futures there's one where ruth  gets in a car accident and one where  ruth has a pulmonary embolism one in  which she finds nadia's dead body  covered in bees which was one of the  deaths she experienced in season one and  one in which she finds alan dead likely  a result of her not being there to  prevent his suicide in season one you  may have also noticed the time periods  crossing over like people from the 1940s  in the background of the hospital in  2022 or alan being able to use his cell  phone in the 1980s the clearest example  of this is nadia's apartment which used  to be a jewish school meshing with her  36th birthday party but it's nadia  finding out ruth has passed and that she  wasn't there for her that puts her over  the edge everything she has done so far  has been for nothing not only was she  unable to change the future but nadia  didn't even get to say goodbye to the  quote best mother she ever had however  she kinda does in the final train  sequence nadia pulls young ruthie aside  and says you had no obligation but you  love me anyway  hi ruthie even though young ruthie has  no idea who she is nadia gets her  goodbye and this time loop finally  closes when nadia comes to the  realization that her past cannot be  separated from who she is as alan says  to her can't escape being the product of  things we can't change this is  symbolized by nadia literally giving  herself over to her mother nadia has  accepted that she can't change the past  and it has given her some closure see in  the end  nothing can absorb us but ourselves the  same can be said of alan who traveled  back in time in the form of his  grandmother to 1962 east berlin there he  found his grandmother involved in a plot  to smuggle people across the berlin wall  but even when he tells his lover lenny  that the wall will eventually fall lenny  still risks his life and goes through  with it no matter what allen did the  outcome would still be the same for  allen this is his coney island if he  could prevent lenny from going across  the wall maybe things would be different  for his grandmother yet whatever he  tried the outcome was the same and lenny  leaves when allen and nadia realize  their pasts can't be undone they're both  hit by a train and sent to the void a  pocket where time doesn't exist it is  here nadia is confronted with a choice  she sees a baby and a bag full of coins  however she only has the strength to  carry one does she choose herself as  signified by the baby or her trauma as  signified by the gold it's this scene  that she literally lets go of her trauma  and chooses herself allen has a final  talk with his grandmother agnes who  gives him a pep talk saying that he  needs to stop worrying and learn to live  even though he may have imperfections to  her he is perfect there's not much we  know about agnes whether this is  actually her or some figment of allen's  imagination but she seems to be someone  who can travel through the timelines and  has an age considering she would have  been born in the 1930s or 40s the name  agnes comes from greek meaning pure and  holy she guides people through the  underground like how she helps nadia in  episode 3. religious and mythological  symbolism is used heavily throughout the  series even nadia is directed by literal  guardian angels when she first emerges  from the train with nadia's arc complete  she emerges back in present day a month  after her 40th birthday ruthie has  passed but nadia has now come to terms  with her death and is at peace with  herself just take a look at the last  shot of season 2 compared with the first  shot of season 1. we've come full circle  however this time nadia is trying ever  so slightly to smile finally having  gained control of her life but what did  you think of russian doll season 2. i  want to hear your thoughts and theories  in the comments below be sure to like  and subscribe and for more bad takes you  can follow me on twitter and instagram  at thingstoryyt until next time remember  nadia you cannot uncook that baby's just  bring it

